From 7308e33293c2312a4dddf4b1846cb7b63e3cd043 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:15:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the pinned message opens with a transition, and the
 composer has a scrollbar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo proposal §6.66, asks 91 and 96 (2026-11-22). Two changes to the two
places a user message is read while it is long.

The pinned card (0102, 0109, 0134) swapped its body instantly when the
toggle expanded it. It now fades in while its body grows from the
minimized row to its 160 px cap, over 150 ms with an ease-out, so a short
message reaches its natural height early in the curve and stops growing.
§6.52 ruled height animations out because the conversation list would lay
out again on every frame; that holds for list items, not here: the pinned
card is an absolute overlay outside the list, and the only thing that
follows its height is the tasks card, which already reads
`top_overlay_bottom` every prepaint. GPUI's `with_animation` draws a
one-shot animation at its end state under reduce motion, so the setting is
honoured without code of ours. Collapsing stays instant. The animation's
element id carries the entry index; a collapsed card renders no expanded
body, so its state is dropped and the next expand starts again from the
row.

The composer had no scrollbar at all, normal or expanded: `Editor::new`
turns scrollbars on only for a full-mode editor, once, and the composer is
built in auto-height mode (`set_mode` never revisits it); and its
EditorStyle left `scrollbar_width` at 0, which makes the editor lay out no
scrollbar. MessageEditor::new now turns the vertical scrollbar on, and the
style sets ui::EDITOR_SCROLLBAR_WIDTH -- only while the draft has more rows
than the composer shows (composer_scrollbar_width). The Xvfb proof found
why: with the width always set, every composer and every sent message (they
share MessageEditor) drew an empty track and a cursor marker on the right.
Visibility then follows the user's `scrollbar.show`, as in any editor.
Known limit, upstream's: an auto-height editor computes its wrap width
without the scrollbar's margin (compute_auto_height_layout), so in the
normal composer the scrollbar may overlay the last column; the expanded
(full-mode) composer reserves the margin.

Tests:
- thread_view::tests::pinned_expand_tests (new; pin_a_message is shared
  from pinned_avatar_tests): expanding_grows_from_the_minimized_row (the
  first frame is no taller than the minimized body plus 4 px, the card is
  open after 400 ms -- Red seen: "the first expanded frame is 163px, the
  minimized body 20px"), reduce_motion_expands_at_once and
  collapsing_is_instant (guards: they hold before and after).
- message_editor::scrollbar_tests (new):
  the_composer_reserves_a_vertical_scrollbar -- in the full-mode composer a
  600-word paragraph wraps into more rows with `scrollbar.show = always`
  than with `never`. Red seen with the style width at 0 (rows equal).
  a_draft_that_fits_gets_no_scrollbar: no width for a draft that fits or
  is not laid out yet. Red seen with the width always set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

